Falsifies `extensible_host_controller_interface::verification::the_event_ring_stays_in_bounds_and_flips_only_at_the_wrap`.

The defect: `EventRing::advance` wraps when the index passes the segment (`>`) instead of when it
reaches the end (`==`). The consumer then stands one entry past the segment and the cycle flips a
step late, so it reads memory the controller never writes and mistakes the next lap for the last.

Expected to fail: the harness's first assertion, `assert!(ring.dequeue < entries)`, from the state
where the index is on the last entry.

diff --git a/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/ring.rs b/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/ring.rs
index c0d58366d..65e0d6074 100644
--- a/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/ring.rs
+++ b/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/ring.rs
@@ -168,7 +168,7 @@ impl EventRing {
     /// Name: ratified 2026-10-25 (#2720).
     pub fn advance(&mut self) {
         self.dequeue += 1;
-        if self.dequeue == self.entries {
+        if self.dequeue > self.entries {
             self.dequeue = 0;
             self.cycle = !self.cycle;
         }
